course: dictionary
lesson: 8518
title: Saturday and the week
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A day is a word that names part of the week, like Monday or Saturday. Saturday is the sixth day of the week, and it comes after Friday and before Sunday. Read the words around a day name to see what it tells you. «On Saturday nine turned up at the door.» The word On comes before the day, so Saturday means one particular day, not every Saturday.
explain: Some sentences mean more than one Saturday. «Halloween, 31 October 2026, is a Saturday, and Bonfire Night, 5 November, is 5 days later, on a Thursday.» Count the days yourself: from Saturday, 5 days later is Thursday. That is a useful check for time problems in maths.
explain: Saturday and Sunday together make the weekend, when most children have no school. Look for clues like «a Saturday job» or «Saturday morning cartoons». Here Saturday tells you when or what kind of job or show, not a new meaning of the word.
explain: Some religions have their own special day, which can change the meaning of the word in a sentence. «The Sabbath is a day of rest and worship; most Christians keep Sunday, … and Jews keep Saturday.» So Saturday is a holy day for Jews. When a text talks about worship, look at the words around it to understand which day it means.
fact: Saturday is a day of the week.
fact: Saturday comes after Friday and before Sunday.
fact: Saturday and Sunday make the weekend.
fact: «On Saturday» means one particular Saturday, and «on Saturdays» means every Saturday.
fact: Saturday is a holy day for Jews, called the Sabbath, a day of rest and worship.
exercise: Which day of the week comes after Friday? | *Saturday | Thursday | Sunday | Monday
exercise: «Halloween, 31 October 2026, is a Saturday.» Which day of the week was Halloween that year? | *Saturday | Friday | Sunday | Thursday
exercise: Saturday and Sunday together make the what? | Month | *Weekend | Holiday | Term
test: «Bonfire Night, 5 November, is 5 days later, on a Thursday.» In that same year, which day was Halloween? | Sunday | Friday | *Saturday | Wednesday
test: Jess has a Saturday job. Which two days make the weekend? | Monday and Tuesday | Friday and Monday | Wednesday and Thursday | *Saturday and Sunday
exam: Which phrase means the Saturday that is coming soon? | a Saturday job | on Saturdays | *this Saturday | Saturday morning cartoons
